// showroom_floor.mat — see CONTRIBUTING.md "Filament runtime ↔ .filamat ABI invariant"
//
// Purpose:    The floor of the model viewer's studio showroom. One large lit quad under
//             the subject: a satin floor that carries the studio's light as a soft sheen,
//             a pool of light under the subject that falls off towards the edges, and the
//             screen-space ambient occlusion of the subject on both its diffuse and its sheen.
//             The far floor is never seen as an edge: the view's height fog carries it into
//             the backdrop colour well before the quad ends, so the floor and the backdrop
//             read as one seamless cyclorama.
// Used by:    samples/android-demo ModelViewerDemo (ShowroomStage) — nothing in the SDK.
// Parameters:
//   centerColor — float3, linear diffuse albedo right under the subject.
//   rimColor    — float3, linear diffuse albedo far from it.
//   poolRadius  — float, floor widths. Height of the virtual lamp the pool falls off from: the
//                 pool is centerColor at the subject, about halfway to rimColor at
//                 0.77 * poolRadius, and gone by about 3 * poolRadius.
//   roughness   — float [0,1], gloss of the floor.
//   reflectance — float [0,1], dielectric Fresnel at normal incidence (0.5 = 4 %).
//   glossRadius — float, floor widths. Radius of the polished zone around the subject: the floor
//                 reflects at full strength under the subject, half-way to rimSpecular at
//                 glossRadius.
//   rimSpecular — float [0,1], what is left of the floor's reflection far from the subject.
//   reflection          — sampler2d, the subject's mirror image (ShowroomReflection): the
//                         subject rendered from the eye mirrored under the floor, alpha =
//                         coverage, linear and pre-exposed like this floor's own colour.
//   reflectionMatrix    — mat4, floor model space -> that mirror render's clip space.
//   reflectionFootprint — float4, the subject's footprint: half width, half depth (floor
//                         widths), cos and sin of its yaw.
//   reflectionEye       — float4, the eye: x and z (floor widths, from the subject's centre),
//                         height above the floor (metres), and how far inside the footprint
//                         the reflection fades out (floor widths).
//   reflectionShape     — float4, strength (0 = off, no texture read), the height on the
//                         subject at which its reflection has faded out (metres), and one
//                         texel of the mirror image (1/width, 1/height).
//   Distances are in the floor's model space — the unit quad, scaled to FLOOR_SIZE_RADII
//   subject radii — but where a parameter says metres.
// matc profile: mobile-only, OpenGL + Vulkan — demo APK asset, not an AAR asset.
//
// Why a material and not a PlaneNode with a colour instance: the pool and the polished zone
// are computed from the model-space position (the floor node sits under the subject's
// centre), so they need no texture and no UVs — and the SDK's colour materials leave the
// specular occlusion off.
//
// The pool profile is the inverse-cube falloff of a lamp at height `poolRadius` over a flat
// floor, (1 + (d/h)^2)^-1.5 — the shape a real spotlight leaves on the ground, so it reads
// as light rather than as a painted vignette.
//
// Why the reflection fades out (glossRadius, rimSpecular): a low camera sees the floor in
// front of the subject at a grazing angle, where it mirrors the studio's bright light strips
// — a hard white band across the bottom of the frame that has nothing to do with the
// subject. Only the polished turntable under the subject keeps the full reflection; the rest
// of the floor reads as satin. `specularFactor` scales the IBL's reflection; Filament only
// keeps the dielectric F0 when `specularColorFactor` is written too, hence the neutral white
// one.
//
// Why `specularAmbientOcclusion`: the IBL does not know the subject stands on the floor, so
// right under a car the floor would still mirror the studio's overhead light — a bright sheen
// where the body should block it. Simple specular occlusion derives the sheen's occlusion
// from the screen-space ambient occlusion, so the sheen dies in the subject's shadow too.
//
// The subject's reflection is planar: ShowroomReflection renders the subject alone, from the
// eye mirrored under the floor, into a small texture whenever the subject or the camera
// moves, and the floor adds it after lighting (postLightingColor, "transparent" blending:
// the mirror image covers the floor by its alpha). Like a real polished showroom floor seen
// from a low camera, it mirrors the wheels and the sills and fades out a little higher up
// the subject (reflectionShape.y), blurring as it fades; inside the footprint it gives way
// to the contact shadow, so no underbody is ever mirrored. Post-lighting colour is added
// before the fog, so the far reflection dissolves into the horizon with the floor.
//
// Why not screen-space reflections: Filament traces them for every pixel of the floor in a
// pass of its own, and a ray that misses — most of them, over a floor — marches to the
// view's maxDistance. Measured on a Pixel 4a (Adreno 618) with the Peugeot 2008: ~360 ms a
// frame, and still 100 ms with the coarsest stride and a trace zone around the subject,
// against 33 ms without. The planar mirror draws the subject a second time, at 40 % of the
// view's size, and only when something moved.
material {
    "name" : "Showroom Floor",
    "parameters" : [
        { "type" : "float3", "name" : "centerColor" },
        { "type" : "float3", "name" : "rimColor" },
        { "type" : "float",  "name" : "poolRadius" },
        { "type" : "float",  "name" : "roughness" },
        { "type" : "float",  "name" : "reflectance" },
        { "type" : "float",  "name" : "glossRadius" },
        { "type" : "float",  "name" : "rimSpecular" },
        { "type" : "sampler2d", "name" : "reflection", "format" : "float", "precision" : "medium" },
        { "type" : "mat4",   "name" : "reflectionMatrix", "precision" : "high" },
        { "type" : "float4", "name" : "reflectionFootprint", "precision" : "high" },
        { "type" : "float4", "name" : "reflectionEye", "precision" : "high" },
        { "type" : "float4", "name" : "reflectionShape" }
    ],
    "requires" : [ "position" ],
    "variables" : [ "floorPosition" ],
    "shadingModel" : "lit",
    "blending" : "opaque",
    "postLightingBlending" : "transparent",
    "specularAmbientOcclusion" : "simple",
    "doubleSided" : false
}
vertex {
    void materialVertex(inout MaterialVertexInputs material) {
        material.floorPosition = float4(getPosition().xyz, 0.0);
    }
}
fragment {
    void material(inout MaterialInputs material) {
        prepareMaterial(material);

        highp float h = max(materialParams.poolRadius, 1e-4);
        highp float q = length(variable_floorPosition.xz) / h;
        highp float k = 1.0 / (1.0 + q * q);
        float pool = k * sqrt(k);

        highp float g = length(variable_floorPosition.xz) / max(materialParams.glossRadius, 1e-4);
        float gloss = 1.0 / (1.0 + g * g);

        material.baseColor = float4(mix(materialParams.rimColor, materialParams.centerColor, pool), 1.0);
        material.metallic = 0.0;
        material.roughness = materialParams.roughness;
        material.reflectance = materialParams.reflectance;
        material.specularColorFactor = float3(1.0);
        material.specularFactor = mix(materialParams.rimSpecular, 1.0, gloss);

        // The subject's mirror image (see the header): where it covers the floor, and how much.
        material.postLightingColor = float4(0.0);
        float4 shape = materialParams.reflectionShape;
        if (shape.x > 0.0) {
            highp float4 clip = materialParams.reflectionMatrix * float4(variable_floorPosition.xyz, 1.0);
            if (clip.w > 0.0) {
                highp float2 uv = uvToRenderTargetUV(clip.xy / clip.w * 0.5 + 0.5);
                highp float2 p = variable_floorPosition.xz;
                highp float4 footprint = materialParams.reflectionFootprint;
                // Into the subject's own frame, then the signed distance to its footprint.
                highp float2 local = float2(footprint.z * p.x - footprint.w * p.y,
                        footprint.w * p.x + footprint.z * p.y);
                highp float2 outside = abs(local) - footprint.xy;
                highp float edge = length(max(outside, 0.0)) + min(max(outside.x, outside.y), 0.0);
                highp float4 eye = materialParams.reflectionEye;
                highp float run = max(length(eye.xz - p), 1e-6);
                // Height on the subject this floor point mirrors: the reflected ray climbs at
                // the eye's slope from here to the footprint's outline.
                float height = max(edge, 0.0) * eye.y / run;
                float fade = min(1.0, height / max(shape.y, 1e-6));
                float weight = shape.x * (1.0 - fade) * (1.0 - fade) * smoothstep(-eye.w, 0.0, edge);
                if (weight > 0.0) {
                    // Sharp where the subject meets the floor, softer as the image fades.
                    float2 r = mix(0.5, 3.0, fade) * shape.zw;
                    float4 c = textureLod(materialParams_reflection, uv, 0.0) * 0.4;
                    c += textureLod(materialParams_reflection, uv + float2( r.x,  r.y), 0.0) * 0.15;
                    c += textureLod(materialParams_reflection, uv + float2(-r.x,  r.y), 0.0) * 0.15;
                    c += textureLod(materialParams_reflection, uv + float2( r.x, -r.y), 0.0) * 0.15;
                    c += textureLod(materialParams_reflection, uv + float2(-r.x, -r.y), 0.0) * 0.15;
                    material.postLightingColor = c * weight;
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
